node_modules/

# dist/ is NOT ignored, though it is a build artifact and everything else of
# that kind in this repo is. It is the one the binary cannot be built without:
# pcomm-ui embeds it, so a source tree with no dist/ cannot produce `pcomm ui`
# at all, and neither can a spack build, which fetches this repo and has no
# pnpm. Committing it is what makes the UI installable for the case it exists
# to serve: capture on a cluster, copy the directory home, read it locally.
# Rebuild with `pnpm -C ui build` and commit the result when the frontend
# changes.
